# pop'n music 9: test mode > e-AMUSEMENT OPTIONS > e-AMUSEMENT ON, SAVE AND EXIT. The game then
# asks for a power cycle; run oracle/scripts/popn9-cardcheck.his with the same --nvram next.
#   hiraku-popn9 --nvram DIR --script oracle/scripts/popn9-eamuse-on.his
game popn9
at 3200 press "Test" 8
at 3320 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3340 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3360 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3380 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3400 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3420 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3440 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3460 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3520 press "P1 Button 5" 10
at 3640 hold "P1 Button 5"
at 3660 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3690 release "P1 Button 5"
at 3740 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3760 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3780 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3800 press "P1 Button 6" 10
at 3840 press "P1 Button 5" 10   # SAVE AND EXIT
at 4100 quit
